"""COURSE AGENT brain, course-scoped for the SKKU Course Agent backend.

Ported from the standalone ``kingo-voice-agent`` repository. Behaviour is
unchanged apart from four integration points:

* answers are generated by this project's ``LLMService`` (Claude, or the
  deterministic mock) instead of the upstream xAI chat model, so the whole
  product has one answer-generation boundary and one configuration surface.
  Only the realtime speech-to-speech leg still runs on xAI Grok, because
  Claude has no realtime voice API.
* ``search_course_materials`` retrieves through the existing course-scoped
  ``RagService`` (pgvector) instead of re-indexing a private PDF folder, so
  sources keep the ``filename p.page`` shape professors already see.
* the trusted-web allowlist and the conversation history are per course and per
  user instead of process-global.
* weak-concept memory is keyed by the authenticated user id.
"""

